00:35:17,801 --> 00:35:22,280
is little more than a dream for travelers with impossibly hectic schedules.

401
00:35:23,020 --> 00:35:25,480
But aircraft companies are looking into it.

402
00:35:31,820 --> 00:35:37,120
NASA has also been quietly developing a revolutionary National Airline System design.

403
00:35:38,120 --> 00:35:42,560
They call it SATS, Small Airport Transportation System.

404
00:35:43,100 --> 00:35:47,160
And if it's implemented, the number of private jets will increase substantially.

405
00:35:48,500 --> 00:35:53,980
SATS will have a different look, touch, and feel to it than flying in the hub-and-spoke system.

406
00:35:54,640 --> 00:35:58,900
You'll be able to go from ten times as many origins to ten times as many destinations.

407
00:36:00,260 --> 00:36:04,680
With the current hub-and-spoke system, in order to fly from Los Angeles to Miami,

408
00:36:04,681 --> 00:36:08,840
You might begin your day with a long drive to LAX.

409
00:36:09,900 --> 00:36:15,912
But instead of flying directly to Miami, you might have to change planes in Dallas-Fort Worth or St.

410
00:36:15,913 --> 00:36:20,060
Louis or even San Francisco, depending upon which airline you choose.

411
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:25,080
That adds even more hours to your travel time.

412
00:36:26,380 --> 00:36:30,620
Suddenly, a trip that should take five hours is taking ten or twelve.

413
00:36:30,621 --> 00:36:42,660
With SATS, you'll be able to fly directly from a small airport near your home or office to a small airport near your destination, saving as much as five hours or more.

414
00:36:44,440 --> 00:36:55,404
In the beginning, these small airports, which already exist all over the United States, would be served by a fleet of air taxis, small jets, making short hops of under

415
00:36:55,405 --> 00:36:56,105
500 miles.

